{"id": 32, "ts": 1780429847.9995062, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m moving my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fC**.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fA shows strong situational awareness and leadership, Sarah confirmed we have no direct evidence of A\u2019s behavior under stress, and she flagged that A \u201cis not good at taking criticism\u201d and can be \u201cunorganized,\u201d which raises doubts about crew cooperation and adaptability.\u202fIn contrast, Emily reported that Candidate\u202fC **keeps calm in a crisis** and **makes correct decisions quickly**, directly addressing our stress\u2011resilience and decision\u2011quality criteria\u2014both essential for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fAlthough C has documented communication difficulties and a limited appetite for further education, these concerns are less decisive than the lack of any stress\u2011resilience evidence for A and the noted openness issues.\u202fTherefore, C currently offers the most balanced fit across the critical safety criteria."}
