{"id": 39, "ts": 1780429880.366608, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification that we lack concrete evidence of Candidate\u202fA\u2019s operational reliability or crew\u2011cooperation, and that the only related notes are a tendency toward being unorganized and difficulty accepting criticism. Those concerns directly touch two of our core criteria\u2014reliability and teamwork\u2014because an unorganized pilot can miss procedural steps, and resistance to feedback undermines cockpit coordination.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s record shows very strong reliability (very conscientious) and solid stress resilience, and while we have a note about a pretentious demeanor and occasional tone issues, those are isolated communication quirks that can be mitigated with targeted onboarding. Given the current evidence, Candidate\u202fB still offers the most balanced fit across reliability, stress handling, and technical competence, with only manageable concerns about professional communication.\nTherefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fB**."}
