{"id": 50, "ts": 1780429918.970017, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m less convinced that Candidate\u202fA is the best fit now that we\u2019ve confirmed there\u2019s no direct evidence of his stress\u2011resilience or decision\u2011making under pressure. Anticipating danger and seeing complex connections are valuable, but without proof he can stay calm and make sound choices when a crisis hits, we can\u2019t rely on those traits alone for long\u2011haul flights.\nBy contrast, Candidate\u202fC is documented as \u201c100\u202f% reliable,\u201d \u201cmakes correct decisions quickly,\u201d and \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew.\u201d Those points give us concrete evidence of decision quality, reliability, and crew cooperation\u2014key for safety\u2011critical, long\u2011distance operations. While his communication style is a concern, the positive crew atmosphere suggests he can still work effectively with others, and his willingness to make fast, correct decisions directly addresses the stress\u2011resilience gap we see with A.\nGiven the current evidence, I would move my vote to Candidate\u202fC as the stronger overall fit."}
